HAVE_SMP	y	32-bit architecture: defined only under arch/arm/, not part of the arm64 configuration (ARMv7 CPU feature)
HAVE_UID16	y	no prompt under arm64: an internal capability flag that only another option can select; the arm64 architecture does not select it. Nothing to choose (16-bit UID system calls of the 32-bit ABI)
HIGHMEM	y	32-bit architecture: defined only under arch/arm/, not part of the arm64 configuration: high memory of the 32-bit kernel. arm64 has none: the whole 3 GiB is mapped directly
HIGHPTE	y	32-bit architecture: defined only under arch/arm/, not part of the arm64 configuration: high memory of the 32-bit kernel. arm64 has none: the whole 3 GiB is mapped directly
IRQSTACKS	y	32-bit architecture: defined only under arch/arm/, not part of the arm64 configuration (ARMv7 CPU feature)
KERNEL_XZ	y	the XZ-compressed 32-bit zImage: needs HAVE_KERNEL_XZ, which arm64 does not set  Kconfig: depends on HAVE_KERNEL_XZ
KMAP_LOCAL	y	no prompt under arm64: an internal capability flag that only another option can select; the arm64 architecture does not select it. Nothing to choose
KMAP_LOCAL_NON_LINEAR_PTE_ARRAY	y	no prompt under arm64: an internal capability flag that only another option can select; the arm64 architecture does not select it. Nothing to choose
KUSER_HELPERS	y	kuser helpers of the 32-bit user ABI: offered only inside `if COMPAT`, and COMPAT stays off
MCPM	y	32-bit architecture: defined only under arch/arm/, not part of the arm64 configuration. The 32-bit port's cluster power management (arch/arm/mach-exynos/mcpm-exynos.c): a cluster powers down and up as a whole, and turns its CCI port on when it comes up. The arm64 port needs its own (SMP workstream)
