MODULES_USE_ELF_REL	y	no prompt under arm64: an internal capability flag that only another option can select; the arm64 architecture does not select it. Nothing to choose (arm64 modules use RELA relocations: MODULES_USE_ELF_RELA, new =y)
NEED_SRCU_NMI_SAFE	y	no prompt under arm64: an internal capability flag that only another option can select; the arm64 architecture does not select it. Nothing to choose (needs an NMI controller; the Exynos 5433 has none)
NEON	y	32-bit architecture: defined only under arch/arm/, not part of the arm64 configuration: the 32-bit FPU and SIMD switches. arm64 has them always; the kernel may use NEON (KERNEL_MODE_NEON, new =y)
NET_VENDOR_CIRRUS	y	`depends on ARM || COMPILE_TEST`: a vendor menu. No device under it is enabled in the release
NET_VENDOR_FARADAY	y	`depends on ARM || COMPILE_TEST`: a vendor menu. No device under it is enabled in the release
OLD_SIGACTION	y	no prompt under arm64: an internal capability flag that only another option can select; the arm64 architecture does not select it. Nothing to choose (old 32-bit signal ABIs)
OLD_SIGSUSPEND3	y	no prompt under arm64: an internal capability flag that only another option can select; the arm64 architecture does not select it. Nothing to choose (old 32-bit signal ABIs)
OUTER_CACHE	y	32-bit architecture: defined only under arch/arm/, not part of the arm64 configuration: the L2 cache controller driver of the 32-bit multi-platform kernel (L2C-210/220/310; the Exynos 5433 does not use it)
