PERF_USE_VMALLOC	y	no prompt under arm64: an internal capability flag that only another option can select; the arm64 architecture does not select it. Nothing to choose
PINCTRL_EXYNOS_ARM	y	prompt only `if COMPILE_TEST` on arm64: selectable, deliberately not enabled (COMPILE_TEST stays off). The ARMv7 pinctrl driver: the same compatibles as PINCTRL_EXYNOS_ARM64 (unchanged =y), which the arm64 kernel uses; building both would make two drivers claim one node
PL353_SMC	y	`depends on ARM || COMPILE_TEST`, `default y if ARM`: the ARM PL353 static memory controller, which the Exynos 5433 does not have
S5P_DEV_MFC	y	no prompt under arm64: an internal capability flag that only another option can select; the arm64 architecture does not select it. Nothing to choose (platform device helper of the 32-bit Samsung machine code, for the MFC video codec)
SAMSUNG_MC	y	prompt only `if COMPILE_TEST` on arm64: selectable, deliberately not enabled (COMPILE_TEST stays off). It is only the menu that offers EXYNOS_SROM and the 5422 memory controller, neither on this board
SELECT_MEMORY_MODEL	y	memory model choice: only with ARCH_SELECT_MEMORY_MODEL, which arm64 does not set
SMP_ON_UP	y	32-bit architecture: defined only under arch/arm/, not part of the arm64 configuration (ARMv7 CPU feature)
SND_ARM	y	32-bit only: `depends on ARM`: sound devices of 32-bit ARM boards. None on the Exynos 5433
