SOC_EXYNOS5410	y	32-bit architecture: defined only under arch/arm/, not part of the arm64 configuration (arch/arm/mach-exynos): selects the SoC's 32-bit machine code. On arm64 the SoC is ARCH_EXYNOS (unchanged =y) and its clock units come from EXYNOS_ARM64_COMMON_CLK (unchanged =y)
SOC_EXYNOS5420	y	32-bit architecture: defined only under arch/arm/, not part of the arm64 configuration (arch/arm/mach-exynos): selects the SoC's 32-bit machine code. On arm64 the SoC is ARCH_EXYNOS (unchanged =y) and its clock units come from EXYNOS_ARM64_COMMON_CLK (unchanged =y)
SOC_EXYNOS5433	y	32-bit architecture: defined only under arch/arm/, not part of the arm64 configuration (arch/arm/mach-exynos): selects the SoC's 32-bit machine code. On arm64 the SoC is ARCH_EXYNOS (unchanged =y) and its clock units come from EXYNOS_ARM64_COMMON_CLK (unchanged =y)
SOC_EXYNOS5800	y	32-bit architecture: defined only under arch/arm/, not part of the arm64 configuration (arch/arm/mach-exynos): selects the SoC's 32-bit machine code. On arm64 the SoC is ARCH_EXYNOS (unchanged =y) and its clock units come from EXYNOS_ARM64_COMMON_CLK (unchanged =y)
SRAM_EXEC	y	no prompt under arm64: an internal capability flag that only another option can select; the arm64 architecture does not select it. Nothing to choose (execute code from SRAM: 32-bit suspend paths)
SWP_EMULATE	y	32-bit architecture: defined only under arch/arm/, not part of the arm64 configuration: emulation of the SWP/SWPB instructions of older ARM ABIs
SYS_SUPPORTS_APM_EMULATION	y	32-bit architecture: defined only under arch/arm/, not part of the arm64 configuration (ARMv7 CPU feature)
UID16	y	16-bit UID system calls: need HAVE_UID16, which arm64 does not set  Kconfig: depends on HAVE_UID16 && MULTIUSER
UNWINDER_ARM	y	32-bit architecture: defined only under arch/arm/, not part of the arm64 configuration: the 32-bit stack unwinder. arm64 uses frame pointers (FRAME_POINTER, new =y)
USE_OF	y	32-bit architecture: defined only under arch/arm/, not part of the arm64 configuration: boot plumbing of the 32-bit zImage (ATAGS, self-relocation, flat tree switch). The arm64 Image takes the device tree and is relocated by its own head code
VDSO	y	32-bit architecture: defined only under arch/arm/, not part of the arm64 configuration: the 32-bit vDSO. The arm64 vDSO is built unconditionally
VFP	y	32-bit architecture: defined only under arch/arm/, not part of the arm64 configuration: the 32-bit FPU and SIMD switches. arm64 has them always; the kernel may use NEON (KERNEL_MODE_NEON, new =y)
VFPv3	y	32-bit architecture: defined only under arch/arm/, not part of the arm64 configuration: the 32-bit FPU and SIMD switches. arm64 has them always; the kernel may use NEON (KERNEL_MODE_NEON, new =y)
VMSPLIT_3G	y	32-bit architecture: defined only under arch/arm/, not part of the arm64 configuration: the 3 GiB / 1 GiB split the release chose so that 32-bit Android (Waydroid) gets 3 GiB of user address space. A 64-bit kernel has no such split
